{'symbol': 'WMT', 'date': '2020-08-18 09:30:00', 'title': 'Walmart Reports Q2 GAAP EPS Of $2.27', 'text': "WALMART QUARTERLY GAAP EPS OF $2.27.QUARTERLY ADJUSTED EPS $1.56.QUARTERLY TOTAL REVENUE WAS $137.7 BILLION, UP $7.4 BILLION.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.25, REVENUE VIEW $135.48 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SAYS EXCLUDING CURRENCY, TOTAL REVENUE WOULD HAVE INCREASED 7.5% TO REACH $140.2 BILLION IN QUARTER.QUARTERLY WALMART U.S. COMP SALES, WITHOUT FUEL, INCREASED 9.3%.QUARTERLY WALMART U.S. ECOMMERCE SALES GREW 97%.QUARTERLY SAM'S CLUB COMP SALES INCREASED 13.3%.QUARTERLY TOTAL U.S. COMPARABLE SALES, WITHOUT FUEL, UP 9.9%.Q2 ADJUSTED. EPS EXCLUDES EFFECTS, NET OF TAX, OF UNREALIZED GAIN OF $0.89 ON EQUITY INVESTMENTS, $0.10 BUSINESS RESTRUCTURING CHARGE IN U.S., $0.08 FOR DISCRETE TAX ITEM.SAYS INCREASED DEMAND FOR PRODUCTS ACROSS MULTIPLE CATEGORIES LED TO STRONG TOP-LINE AND GROSS MARGIN RESULTS IN QUARTER.SAYS COMPANY INCURS INCREMENTAL COSTS RELATED TO COVID-19 OF $1.5 BILLION.SAYS REDUCED QTRLY TOBACCO SALES NEGATIVELY AFFECTED SAM'S CLUB COMP SALES BY ABOUT 390 BASIS POINTS.SAYS IN QUARTER, NEW MEMBER COUNT FOR SAM'S CLUB INCREASED MORE THAN 60%."}
